{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/oxlint/configuration_schema.json",
  "plugins": ["typescript"],
  // The TYPE-AWARE lint pass (oxlint --type-aware, powered by oxlint-tsgolint/tsgo).
  // It replaced the old ESLint + typescript-eslint pass — same idea, no tsc.
  //
  // STRICTNESS RATCHET (WS-H1, rule-by-rule). The `correctness` category — the
  // highest-value typed bug-catchers — is now ON at error. Its rules
  // (`no-base-to-string`, `restrict-template-expressions`,
  // `no-redundant-type-constituents`) were triaged to zero and the surfaced code
  // FIXED (a `[object Object]`-stringification class on raw pg rows + Hono form
  // bodies, a couple of `never`-template guards, two redundant union members) —
  // not silenced. The one correctness rule held OFF is `unbound-method`: every
  // one of its 32 hits is a FALSE POSITIVE on a function-VALUED object property
  // (the credential `refresh: () => Promise<string>` and the poll `sleep`
  // fields), which carries no `this` binding — the rule's heuristic can't tell
  // those from a real class method. It is NOT disabled to dodge work; the rest
  // of the category is at error.
  //
  // STRICTNESS RATCHET (WS-H1b, rule-by-rule). The `suspicious` category is
  // ratcheted the SAME way `correctness` was — not as a category flip, but
  // rule-by-rule, because its dominant rule `no-unsafe-type-assertion` (378 hits,
  // mostly the INTENTIONAL pg-row `as` casts at trusted DB read-seams) is a large
  // standalone effort that wants the typed-row / zod-at-the-seam treatment, not a
  // blanket flip. So the category stays OFF and the TRACTABLE suspicious rules are
  // enabled INDIVIDUALLY at error below, with every surfaced site FIXED (not
  // silenced): the redundant casts/conversions/template-literals/boolean-literal
  // compares were removed at the seam; the `consistent-return` exhaustive switches
  // grew a `never`-asserting `default` (so a new union member is a COMPILE error),
  // and the value-returning org-scoped callbacks made their early `return;` an
  // explicit `return undefined;`. Two suspicious rules are deferred with rationale
  // (NOT to dodge work):
  //   • `no-unsafe-type-assertion` (378) — the pg-row trust-at-boundary effort.
  //     IN PROGRESS (WS-H1c): the typed pg-row READ SEAM landed — the `pgRows.ts`
  //     helper (`queryRawRows`/`requireRow`/`oneOf`) + the `client.query<RawRow>()`
  //     generic retype + zod-enum column decodes cleaned the ENTIRE Repositories /
  //     store seam (repositories/*, notifications/store, forge/{threads,proposals},
  //     dag/integrationNodesPg, auth/identityStore — ~71 casts), so a pg row is now
  //     VALIDATED at the seam (fail-loud) instead of `as`-asserted past it. The rule
  //     stays OFF until the remaining NON-pg-row classes are cleaned the same way —
  //     remaining by area: orchestrator ~238 (HTTP `response.json()` decodes, the
  //     `as never` Hono event writes, jsonb-walk `value as Record<…>` provider
  //     guards, the `orgScopingPool` variadic proxy cast), dashboard ~57 (DOM/React
  //     + client serializers), allocator ~7, cli ~8 (JSON.parse / external input).
  //     Sequenced as follow-up waves (one per non-pg-row class).
  //   • `no-unnecessary-type-parameters` (4) — all 4 are single-use RETURN-position
  //     generics on typed JSON-parse / typed-`query` helpers (`sendJson<T>`,
  //     `safeJson<T>`, `query<R>`, `HonoJson<T>`). The rule's "fix" (drop the
  //     generic → return `unknown` and cast at every call site) would PUSH unsafe
  //     `as` casts out to callers — the opposite of the trust-at-boundary doctrine.
  //
  // The remaining categories stay OFF pending follow-up rule-by-rule ratchets
  // (pedantic/style/restriction/nursery — see the WS-H1 PR body for per-rule
  // finding counts). The 3 original high-value typed rules below stay pinned (they
  // predate the category being on; keeping them explicit documents the floor).
  "categories": {
    "correctness": "error",
    "suspicious": "off",
    "pedantic": "off",
    "perf": "off",
    "style": "off",
    "restriction": "off",
    "nursery": "off"
  },
  "rules": {
    "typescript/no-floating-promises": "error",
    "typescript/no-misused-promises": "error",
    "typescript/await-thenable": "error",
    // FALSE-POSITIVE-only on this codebase (function-valued `refresh`/`sleep`
    // object properties, not class methods). Held off with rationale, not to
    // dodge work — the rest of `correctness` is at error above.
    "typescript/unbound-method": "off",
    // WS-H1b: the tractable `suspicious` rules, enabled rule-by-rule at error with
    // every surfaced site fixed (the `suspicious` category itself stays OFF until
    // the `no-unsafe-type-assertion` pg-row seam wave lands — see the header).
    "typescript/no-unnecessary-type-assertion": "error",
    "typescript/no-unnecessary-type-conversion": "error",
    "typescript/no-unnecessary-boolean-literal-compare": "error",
    "typescript/no-unnecessary-template-expression": "error",
    "typescript/no-unnecessary-type-arguments": "error",
    "typescript/consistent-return": "error"
  }
}
